Subject: [PATCH] window: a hidden window on Windows tells its page where it is

A window opened hidden, such as in a disconnected remote desktop session,
never sent its renderer the window rect: RenderWidgetHostImpl skips screen
rects while the widget is hidden. Its page read outerWidth and
outerHeight as the screen's available rect, 1920x1032, from patch 0100,
while the window was 1248x972, so outerWidth - innerWidth was 688.

On Windows a hidden view now sends its rects when it is in a window and
that window is at least as large as the view. A background tab is in no
window and a minimised window is smaller than its view; both still wait
until they are shown, as before.

diff --git a/content/browser/renderer_host/render_widget_host_impl.cc b/content/browser/renderer_host/render_widget_host_impl.cc
index 043cc52..c82dde8 100644
--- a/content/browser/renderer_host/render_widget_host_impl.cc
+++ b/content/browser/renderer_host/render_widget_host_impl.cc
@@ -688,7 +688,25 @@ void RenderWidgetHostImpl::SendScreenRects() {
   if (is_hidden_) {
     // On GTK, this comes in for backgrounded tabs. Ignore, to match what
     // happens on Win & Mac, and when the view is shown it'll call this again.
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN)
+    // Apostate: a window that is hidden from the start, such as one opened
+    // in a disconnected remote session or behind other windows, never told
+    // its renderer where it is, and outerWidth and outerHeight read the
+    // screen's available rect (patch 0100) while the window is smaller. A
+    // view that is in a window, and whose window holds it, sends its rects
+    // while hidden too. A background tab is in no window and a minimised
+    // window is smaller than its view; both still wait to be shown.
+    const gfx::NativeView native_view = view_->GetNativeView();
+    const gfx::Rect view_rect = view_->GetViewBoundsWithoutTransform();
+    const gfx::Rect window_rect = view_->GetBoundsInScreenWithoutTransform();
+    if (!native_view || !native_view->GetRootWindow() || view_rect.IsEmpty() ||
+        window_rect.width() < view_rect.width() ||
+        window_rect.height() < view_rect.height()) {
+      return;
+    }
+#else
     return;
+#endif
   }
 
   if (last_view_screen_rect_ == view_->GetViewBoundsWithoutTransform() &&
